        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-721] After indication of a successful Data-Link establishment (D-LINK_READY.indication(DLINKSTATUS=Link established)), the SECC shall initiate the address assignment mechanism.",
            "block_bbox": [
                67,
                167,
                1052,
                247
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    67.0,
                    167.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    167.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    247.0
                ],
                [
                    67.0,
                    247.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-026] The SECC shall configure an IP address (static or dynamic) by any appropriate mechanism.",
            "block_bbox": [
                69,
                268,
                1052,
                322
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    69.0,
                    268.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    268.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    322.0
                ],
                [
                    69.0,
                    322.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 1 To enable the integration of an SECC in different communication infrastructures, the definition of the address assignment for the SECC is not in the scope of this document. This enables the operator to assign an appropriate mechanism. For example, the operator can choose any existing mechanism providing a valid IP address like, for example, a static IP or the mechanism described in 7.6.3.2 and 7.6.3.3.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                344,
                1053,
                441
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    344.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    344.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    441.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    441.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-027] After the IP address is assigned, the SECC shall start the SDP server as defined in 7.10.1.",
            "block_bbox": [
                69,
                462,
                1053,
                515
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    69.0,
                    462.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    462.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    515.0
                ],
                [
                    69.0,
                    515.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 2 It is not required that the SECC discovery service is implemented in the SECC directly. It is also possible to have a separate unit providing the SECC discovery service.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                536,
                1053,
                588
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    536.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    536.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    588.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    588.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-723] The SECC may stop the SDP server when SECC_CommunicationSetup_Timer is equal or larger than V2G_SECC_CommunicationSetup_Performance_Time.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                608,
                1053,
                665
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    608.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    608.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    665.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    665.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-029] The SECC may stop the IP address assignment mechanism when V2G\\_SECC\\_CommunicationSetup\\_Timer is equal or larger than V2G\\_SECC\\_CommunicationSetup\\_Performance\\_Time.",
            "block_bbox": [
                69,
                683,
                1054,
                764
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
